  "notes": "Cantonese (粵語) romanised input contract: Jyutping (LSHK 1997), not Han characters, exactly as `zh` expects Hanyu Pinyin. Jyutping initials, monophthong/diphthong finals and the six citation-tone digits (1-6, Chao tone letters after Matthews & Yip 1994: 55/35/33/21/13/22) are cited graphemes; each earns its key by test 2 (one segment/tone per spelling unit) or test 1 (digraphs gw/kw/ng/aa/oe/yu/eo are not the concatenation of their letters). Tone is lexical and fully written by the digit, so no separate stress block applies (tonal language exemption, AGENTS.md/quality_tiers.md). Registered against WikiPron's yue_latn_standard_broad gold (Jyutping-romanised Wiktionary entries). ENGINE-LIMIT EXCEPTION: bare digit characters are stripped by the tokenizer input normalisation before matching, so the six tone-digit graphemes above do not currently fire in transcribe() output; they remain a correct cited claim about the Jyutping spelling convention, pending an engine change to accept digit graphemes (a tokenizer gap, not a spec error).",
